        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 15:1",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Sixteen years old was he when he began to reign, and he reigned two and fifty years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jecholiah of Jerusalem.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 123
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 15:2",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And he did that which was right in the sight of the Lord, according to all that his father Amaziah had done;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 25
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 15:3",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 15,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Save that the high places were not removed: the people sacrificed and burnt incense still on the high places.",
